                                "sense_id": "6faf0c63-f9cb-39ac-a067-d9999c64ad87",
                                "text": "Eftir this the Erles and thair kin passis to the Tolbuith, with the haill ministerie: all ar maid burgessis of this toun; the ministers with the rest. At euin^([even]), nathing bot wauchting."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ddf2e39c-b561-4883-9e66-b0280ccacba3",
                                "sense_id": "6faf0c63-f9cb-39ac-a067-d9999c64ad87",
                                "text": "[…]while with Huntly, who in April 1599 had been created Marquis, the King now spent much of his time, “wauchting and drinking.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "28c25a2a-cf6a-42c6-bf28-1785791bc43d",
                                "sense_id": "6faf0c63-f9cb-39ac-a067-d9999c64ad87",
                                "text": "2000, Association for Scottish Literary Studies, Scottish Literary Journal, Volume 27, Issue 1, page 45,\nScott, on the other hand, says of him that he ‘wauchted [quaffed] the bluid-reid liquor doun’."
                            }
